## Roadmap

- [x] `pyproject.toml` for `pip install -e .` with a `cvar-engine` console entry point
- [x] CLI exposing the paper's own experiments (`paper-portfolio`, `nikkei`, `validate`, `figures`)
- [x] GitHub Actions CI running the suite, the paper regression and the figure build
- [x] Table 7 NIKKEI book reconstructed, with implied volatilities inverted from the published marks
- [x] Figure 1 reconstruction, with the normality test the paper's claim implies
- [ ] **Tables 8 and 9** — the one- and four-instrument CVaR hedges. Needs the nonsmooth subgradient solver below, or the equivalent LP over the eq. (23) loss matrix
- [ ] Nonsmooth subgradient solver (Uryasev, 1991), the method the paper actually used in Section 4
- [ ] `notebooks/` with annotated walkthroughs of each of the three layers
- [ ] NSGA-III / MOEA/D reference-direction survival to improve three-objective spread
- [ ] CVaR-constrained variants, and relaxation of the joint-density assumption

