## Academic References

**Primary source — the formulation this engine implements and is validated against:**

> Rockafellar, R. T. and Uryasev, S. (2000). **Optimization of Conditional Value-at-Risk.** *Journal of Risk*, 2(3), 21–41.

Included in this repository as [`rtr179-CVaR1.pdf`](rtr179-CVaR1.pdf). Equations (4), (11), (12), (15) and (17), Theorems 1 and 2, and the Proposition of Section 3 are referenced directly in the source comments.

> **Which parts of this repository come from which source is set out in [Provenance & Attribution](#provenance--attribution).** The works below contribute components the reference paper does not contain — the multi-objective layer, the stress-testing layer, and the discrete-atom CVaR estimator all rest on them rather than on the 2000 paper.

**Supporting literature:**

> Rockafellar, R. T. and Uryasev, S. (2002). **Conditional Value-at-Risk for General Loss Distributions.** *Journal of Banking & Finance*, 26(7), 1443–1471.
>
> Source of the exact discrete-atom CVaR decomposition `CVaR = λ·VaR + (1-λ)·CVaR⁺` used by the historical estimator. The 2000 paper assumes no probability atoms, which does not hold for a finite scenario set.

> Artzner, P., Delbaen, F., Eber, J.-M. and Heath, D. (1999). **Coherent Measures of Risk.** *Mathematical Finance*, 9(3), 203–228.
>
> The axioms motivating CVaR over VaR.

> Markowitz, H. M. (1952). **Portfolio Selection.** *Journal of Finance*, 7(1), 77–91.
>
> The minimum-variance benchmark, problem (P3).

> Mausser, H. and Rosen, D. (1999). **Beyond VaR: From Measuring Risk to Managing Risk.** *ALGO Research Quarterly*, 1(2), 5–20.
>
> Source of the NIKKEI hedging problem in the paper's Section 4.

> Deb, K., Pratap, A., Agarwal, S. and Meyarivan, T. (2002). **A Fast and Elitist Multiobjective Genetic Algorithm: NSGA-II.** *IEEE Transactions on Evolutionary Computation*, 6(2), 182–197.

> Deb, K. and Agrawal, R. B. (1995). **Simulated Binary Crossover for Continuous Search Space.** *Complex Systems*, 9(2), 115–148.

> Das, I. and Dennis, J. E. (1998). **Normal-Boundary Intersection.** *SIAM Journal on Optimization*, 8(3), 631–657.
>
> The simplex-lattice weight design used to sweep the Tchebycheff front.

> Miettinen, K. (1999). **Nonlinear Multiobjective Optimization.** Kluwer Academic Publishers.
>
> Augmented Tchebycheff scalarization theory.

> Zitzler, E. and Thiele, L. (1999). **Multiobjective Evolutionary Algorithms: A Comparative Case Study and the Strength Pareto Approach.** *IEEE Transactions on Evolutionary Computation*, 3(4), 257–271.
>
> Hypervolume and coverage indicators.

> Black, F. and Scholes, M. (1973). **The Pricing of Options and Corporate Liabilities.** *Journal of Political Economy*, 81(3), 637–654.

> Merton, R. C. (1973). **Theory of Rational Option Pricing.** *Bell Journal of Economics and Management Science*, 4(1), 141–183.
>
> Continuous dividend yield in the pricer.

